{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/503158-scroll-of-ages-and-mummy-inaccessibility","id":503158,"title":"Scroll of Ages and Mummy inaccessibility","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-04T11:21:35-07:00","id":503158,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Scroll of Ages and Mummy inaccessibility","content":"First of all, I really like the central concept in Mummy of waking powerful but oblivious to your past, and growing less powerful but more wise as time goes on. It's a great idea to structure any plot consisting revelations and unfolding mysteries around. I also adore the Utterances, the cults, the Shuankhsen antagonists. I like how Sothis Ascends makes a campaign setting for the game and gives you reams of locations and eras to set your game in with hundreds of plothooks.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> My main issue with Mummy is I find the lore inaccessible. I think it's in part a language thing. I'm dyslexic, but I'm not a stupid guy, but with every new book there are new terms being thrown out and I'm struggling to understand them all. It really confused me with Book of the Deceived, as half of the book is too dense for me. Like the writers were referring to such heavy mythology they couldn't explain anything in a straightforward way. This probably makes me sound dim, but I get every other WoD game, and honestly I couldn't read Deceived without having to put it down constantly realizing I'd not understood half of what I'd read. It was like reading course material for an exam on a subject I knew very little about.<br /> <br /> I've spoken to other players who have the same problem and none of them are dyslexic. It's a copout to call them stupid too. They don't want to play Mummy because it's too dense despite the excellent premise. It's not a game you can pick up and play. It's a game you need to study and interpret. This is probably why it gets nominated for awards but I can never find players. It's like an art film. A small group will love it. I love elements, but the game as a whole takes a lot of chewing.<br /> <br /> This takes me to the title of the thread. The Scroll of Ages. In the opening to Mummy it mentions a Scroll of Ages that'd be updated regularly with a lexicon, and other useful features to help us with our games. This would be such a perfect resource for Mummy. It's a little ridiculous that any game needs a reference guide, but it would help a lot of people understand what's on the page.<br /> <br /> Will this Scroll of Ages ever see release? It was something promised when the game was released. Who has the responsibility for developing this feature? Is it something the community were meant to develop as part of the wiki? Is it something C.A. Suleiman was supposed to be doing but never got to?<br /> <br /> If anyone can help me with my queries about the Scroll of Ages, or even if they have the time and will create a lexicon right here on the forum, it'd help me and many others gets a grip on this game that seems to put up barriers for new players.<br /> <br /> One more thing. It probably seems like I should just try harder to get it, but I thought about that and realized this is meant to be a game, and surely anyone should be able to have fun with a game. Just because I'm not the most able reader when it comes to complex language or historical terms with no context doesn't mean I shouldn't be able to play, and again, I've no problem with any other RPG. There's something about Mummy, it's terms, its writing, that seems incredibly inaccessible. Have you found this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:15:55-07:00","id":503295,"title":"","content":"Mummy is rather incredibly dense, yes. I'm not sure that's a fault though.<br /> <br /> I'll comment more when I'm not scrambling to appease my religious scholar overlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:04:05-07:00","id":503582,"title":"","content":"I gave up on the Scroll of Ages a long time ago. I don't think there's even been a hint that it might show up since the core book was released.<br /> <br /> Mummy does have a lot of information and backstory packed into it, but I'm not sure how much is necessary for the players to learn. I have players who have never read the books (outside of the mechanic bits) who get by just fine. They have amnesia, after all.<br /> <br /> Is there anything specific you're having trouble with? &quot;The whole line is inaccessible&quot; is hard to provide meaningful help with, but if there are certain elements in particular that are confusing you then I'm sure the forum can talk you through them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T18:50:08-07:00","id":503719,"title":"","content":"<b>Mage</b> is a game with lots of terms, and I don't think <b>Mummy</b> has more than that. All these games can be pretty dense, though.<br /> <br /> Remember that <b>Book of the Deceived</b> is basically another 'core' book, introducing an entirely new type of playable protagonist. It's only natural for it to be loaded up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T20:14:06-07:00","id":503745,"title":"","content":"It's also packed into a book half the size of a normal core book. They stuffed it to the absolute brim with content. I love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:38:03-07:00","id":503859,"title":"","content":"I didn't find the game inaccessible at all. Once you accept the core premises, I think it's rather easy to come up with plot lines and things to do with the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:40:13-07:00","id":503860,"title":"","content":"I've created a thread whose explicit purpose is giving people ideas what to do with the game; maybe it can help you? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\"> 1001 Mummy Story Hooks - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Reposting my old 1001 Mummy Story Hooks thread here, because that sort of thread tends to be useful. Please be aware that the numbers won't be consecutive - I created this thread on three separate fora. .) The first time a PC increases her Memory, she recalls that her Judge, back in Duat, warned her about </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:01:42-07:00","id":504781,"title":"","content":"You're the amnesiac immortal servants of an ancient Egyptian empire, drawn from the &quot;middle class&quot; and bound to the service of your gods, the 42 Judges.<br /> <br /> That's all anyone needs to go to get the game going. Hell, that's half the reason Memory starts off so low; so that nobody has to start off knowing everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:10:09-07:00","id":504804,"title":"","content":"Yeah, at the starting Memory level all a player needs to know is a rough overview of their Guild, Decree, and Judge, and possibly the word &quot;Irem&quot;. From there, they only really remember their most recent Descent, which precludes knowing most of the more terminology-heavy parts of the backstory.<br /> <br /> And if the players don't know, it's not even something the Storyteller has to know unless they decide to tell stories that specifically draw upon those parts of the setting. And that's the Storyteller's choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T21:56:53-07:00","id":505043,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty accessible as a player, although character concepts don't exactly leap to my head. I'm one of those people who think that Mummy would be pretty frustrating to put together and run. But I have no real experience, so take that with a pinch of salt.<br /> <br /> I don't blame CAS and the writers for the delay on the Scroll of Ages. The guys at OPP have said that we're due to get our wikis and other electronic resources back really soon now since we switched to this forum software. IIRC the people who would implement that are also wearing 2-3 other hats for the company so I can't be -that- mad, but it's frustrating nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T22:46:21-07:00","id":505077,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the Mummy core book contains at least one &quot;not for everyone&quot; disclaimer, but I've never had so much fun running games. The ease at which everything can be made personal for characters is great, and the mechanics do an incredible job of encouraging precisely the kind of behaviour you expect from the characters. High Sekhem Mummies are supremely confident but act almost desperate, racing to complete objectives before they lose power. As they run out of power they begin to act more acclimatised, looking for solutions within the framework of the mundane world. I've got half a dozen character concepts buzzing around my head as well, but I doubt I'll ever get the chance to play them.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I'm sure if the OP posts up the specific elements they're having trouble with, we can sort out those problems pretty easily. At the moment, there's not much more we can do than vague &quot;it's not that hard, particularly if you use Memory as an excuse to ignore most of it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:10:22-07:00","id":511976,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for your input so far. The simplification of the game that a few have posted about is useful, and a good way for me to approach it.<br /> <br /> At this point I'm struggling a little with a the following:<br /> <br /> Duat: Is this something that the players are meant to experience playing through, and if so is there advice on how to run the descent? The Book of the Deceived has a character meeting Anubis. Is this what happens with Arisen, or do they meet their Judge? What power level does a mummy have in Duat?<br /> <br /> Judges: What are the Judges and what's their relationship with the Shan'iatu, gods, Temakh (?) and Azar?<br /> <br /> Temakh: I really struggle to understand what this is. Is it a Judge living in a mummy's sahu (body) like the Shadow in Wraith or Geist? What does it want?<br /> <br /> Shan'iatu: I assume these are the sorcerers who formed the Rite of Return. Why did they do this? If they are not the Judges, what did they gain from allowing their servants immortality? Why did they not grant it to themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:33:28-07:00","id":511986,"title":"","content":"You are not meant to experience playing through Duat. There is a place called Neter-Khertet, which is essentially Twilight, where you end up when you die during a Descent as long as you don't drop to Sekhem 0 as a consequence. That is where you meet Anubis, and the ST half of the corebook has advice for handling that.<br /> <br /> We're still piecing together the Judges and the Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> Temakh are something only the Deceived have, and they are fragments of their Shan'iatu creator. The Sixth Guild's Shan'iatu were betrayed by the others and splintered into fragments which became trapped in the bodies of their Deathless servants. Other Arisen do not have such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T13:51:39-07:00","id":512293,"title":"","content":"<b>Duat</b> is where the Arisen rest between Descents. Nothing ever allows them to remember their time in Duat, not even high Memory. During a death cycle (when they're killed in the middle of a Descent), the Arisen go to <b>Neter-Khertet</b> (Twilight, the sort of invisible realm overlaying the mortal world, where unmanifested ghosts hang out) and sometimes meet with Anpu/Anubis.<br /> <br /> The <b>Shan'iatu </b>were the sorcerer-priest-kings who ran Irem. Each of the Guilds had seven Shan'iatu guildmasters, who led the populace to observe the word of the Judges. <i>Book of the Deceived</i> suggests that they tried to usurp the Judges using the Rite of Return, hoping to become gods; the Arisen were to be their immortal unthinking servants.<br /> <br /> The <b>Judges </b>are the 42 godlike entities that the Arisen exist to serve. The Shan'iatu brought the worship of the Judges to Irem and hoped to join their ranks with magic. Given that they're roughly aligned to the Five Decrees (each of the five are tied to a Nameless God: Re for Falcon-Headed, Esit for Lion-Headed, Ptah for Bull-Headed, Sutek for Serpent-Headed, and Anpu for Jackal-Headed), we don't really know too much about how the Judges connect to the Nameless Gods other than some king of relation. The Nameless Gods are more powerful than them, I believe. Azar is the king of the Nameless Gods.<br /> <br /> <b>Temakh</b> are the shattered spirits of the Shan'iatu who ran the Lost Guild, who were Deceived and denied ascension. They're basically insane ancient ghost-monsters who share mental space with the Deceived, kind of like super-powerful super-crazy geists. They usually want worship and to exact revenge upon the servants of the Judges. The Arisen know nothing of them and almost none of them believe the Lost Guild still exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T15:41:50-07:00","id":512372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/503158-scroll-of-ages-and-mummy-inaccessibility?p=512293#post512293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re for Falcon-Headed, Esit for Lion-Headed</div> </div> </div> </div>Other way around, actually, as weird as it seems to anyone who would assume &quot;Ra&quot; is the falcon.<br /> <br /> Other than that, excellent summary. The only things I would add are the following:<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu are, according to the Book of the Deceived, not human. They didn't need the Rite to become immortal, because they were already immortal. Evidence suggests the Rite was intended to empower them to take up the mantle of godhood (at least on par with the Judges), an ascension rather than a bid to longevity on their part.<br /> <br /> Azar is the king of Duat, so the 42 Judges are subordinate to him. We don't actually know if he is the chief of the Nameless Gods. He is the one the Shan'iatu placed above the others in their own rituals, however, and was the patron god of Irem.<br /> <br /> The nature of the Judges is very complicated and we have some conflicting evidence on what they are. The 42 who rule the Arisen may have been products of the same Rite that created the Arisen, or they could be the original 42 Judges &quot;of Life&quot; who were the parents of the Shan'iatu as described in the Book of the Deceived, manifestations of divine law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T23:16:49-07:00","id":512630,"title":"","content":"One of the relics in the corebook suggests strongly that the Judges of Duat are not the Judges of Life but separate entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T23:27:26-07:00","id":512634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/503158-scroll-of-ages-and-mummy-inaccessibility?p=512630#post512630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the relics in the corebook suggests strongly that the Judges of Duat are not the Judges of Life but separate entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pale Brood? If I remember the wording correctly, you could squint and make an argument for it both ways...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T21:05:31-07:00","id":513755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/503158-scroll-of-ages-and-mummy-inaccessibility?p=512634#post512634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Pale Brood? If I remember the wording correctly, you could squint and make an argument for it both ways...</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a description of a human that became a judge of Duat. We don't have any description of a Judge of Life becoming a Judge of Duat or even directly involving themselves much in what is going on so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T21:40:53-07:00","id":513786,"title":"","content":"Well, the phrasing is something like &quot;the one who would become known as the Eater of Blood&quot;, which doesn't necessarily mean the same thing as &quot;the one who would become the Eater of Blood&quot;. Since I'm pretty sure the developers have suggested that this shouldn't be taken as evidence of the Shan'iatu becoming the Judges, and that the alternative is that a random Su-Menent priest was elevated to godhood, I... generally throw the Pale Brood out the window, cosmologically speaking. It confuses me.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the Book of the Deceived, reference is made to the fact that the Judges of Life descent to Duat to perform the very duties the Judges of Duat perform. Which is hardly conclusive evidence to them being one and the same, of course, but it's about as much evidence as we have for alternative theories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T03:05:49-07:00","id":513993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/503158-scroll-of-ages-and-mummy-inaccessibility?p=513786#post513786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the phrasing is something like &quot;the one who would become known as the Eater of Blood&quot;, which doesn't necessarily mean the same thing as &quot;the one who would become the Eater of Blood&quot;. Since I'm pretty sure the developers have suggested that this shouldn't be taken as evidence of the Shan'iatu becoming the Judges, and that the alternative is that a random Su-Menent priest was elevated to godhood, I... generally throw the Pale Brood out the window, cosmologically speaking. It confuses me.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the Book of the Deceived, reference is made to the fact that the Judges of Life descent to Duat to perform the very duties the Judges of Duat perform. Which is hardly conclusive evidence to them being one and the same, of course, but it's about as much evidence as we have for alternative theories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it means the maker of that object, who does not appear to be a Shan iatu became the Judge known as the Eater of Blood. I did a search for &quot;Judges of Life.&quot; in Deceived and found zero references to them going into Duat. Only references to the ones who became the temakh's wanting to become the Judges of Duat and Life as great as or greater than the Judges of Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T04:42:14-07:00","id":514031,"title":"","content":"&quot;And the Judges had given the Remet five powers, to guide them to a place called Duat, to appear before the 42 for a final destiny in accord with their obedience to the Law.&quot; -Book of the Deceived, page 20, &quot;The Great Beasts&quot;.<br /> <br /> Seems pretty conclusive. The Judges of Life travel to Duat to judge souls, so that those proven worthy may return with them to dwell in Heaven. This predates the Rite by a fairly lengthy period, so I can't see what else &quot;appear before the 42&quot; could possibly mean.<br /> <br /> Like I said though, it isn't definitive proof one way or the other. The Pale Brood could indeed mean to refer to individuals transformed into Judges by the Rite, but it just seems a bit... out of left field, given the nature of the Shan'iatu's plan. Or, alternatively, since we know from Guildhalls of the Deathless that the Judges can create Relics, it's even possible that the Eater of Blood in the story actually refers to one of the Judges of Life before the Rite (presumably lending a somewhat apocryphal bent to the story as a consequence), implying that the name Unem-Sef/Eater of Blood was only given to the Judge <i>after</i> the events described in the story. There's a few different ways to read it, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T11:33:05-07:00","id":514354,"title":"","content":"Here are some fun theories on the 'Judge of Life and Death' thing.<br /> <br /> The Judges are almost certainly the 'The Assessors of Ma'at', who do not have an association strictly speaking with life or death originally. They don't have to travel to Duat to judge souls because in conventional Egyptian (and we must presume Iremite) metaphysics, the Duat is where the Gods hang out. The Gods do NOT live in the paradise intended for human beings (Aa'ru). And indeed, once the Judges find you worthy, it's not a given you'll make it to Aa'ru anyway. They just give you permission to hike there yourself. Which takes many years and involves knife-fighting demons at many gates.<br /> <br /> The Egyptians were pretty metal.<br /> <br /> I think we can safely conclude the following thus far. The things the Guildmasters created are obviously intended as replacements for the judges. These may simply be theological replacements... concepts and ideas that helped unify Irem as a nation and explain the past adaquately... or they may have been functional replacements that in some way altered fundamental metaphysics that were previously a hindrance to the Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> We do not know that the Shan'iatu became the Judges, or even that they ultimately intended to do so. They were primarily concerned with reaching Aa'ru, a place that was forbidden to them. Pay close attention to what Anpu says in Book of the Decieved -<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat god,\u201d I said. \u201cWhat manner of creature passed beyond Neter-Khertet?\u201d<br /> 'A man\u2019s soul.<br /> \u201cGreat god, what is a soul?\u201d<br /> 'The binding of five powers that guides a man through the world of life, into the presence of the Judges and then, life beyond life.'<br /> <br /> The Guildmasters clearly intended to 'hack' this process. They constructed physical embodiments of the Five Powers (the Pillars) and meddled with them until they managed to find something they believed would give them access to Aa'ru.<br /> <br /> Now, for the true horror of this, understand the following...<br /> <br /> The replacements, these Judges of Death which are not in any way the Assessors of Ma'at and have horrible descriptions with lich-like bodies, they let people into the DUAT when they please them. DUAT is actually the lose condition in the old myth. It's where you go if you can't get into Aa'ru, if you don't weigh the same as the feather of Ma'at. It's where bad people and losers go.<br /> <br /> The DUAT is absolutely NOT the paradise the Guildmasters coveted and wanted access to. That's Aa'ru.<br /> <br /> One almost gets the impression that the Shan'iatu wanted in to Paradise, and that they sold out everybody... and everything... to get it. They used supernatural necromancy to effectively steal heaven. Awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:16:32-07:00","id":514486,"title":"","content":"Is the Sky Beyond The Sky then Aa'ru?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T12:15:25-07:00","id":515340,"title":"","content":"Not sure what the Sky Beyond the Sky is, educate me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T16:21:06-07:00","id":515576,"title":"","content":"A'aru, the Light Land, Heaven, and the Sky Beyond the Sky all seem different terms for the same place, yes.<br /> <br /> Regarding the whole &quot;the Judges seem too horrifying to be 'Judges of Life'&quot; theory though, our only description of the Judges of Life states &quot;They were horrors at the threshold of knowing: beauty so profound that to finite beings, they could only arouse fear. And it is right to worship what one fears.&quot; Lovecraftian entities seem like a pretty valid way for humans to conceive of such beings...<br /> <br /> Another interesting fact is that Azar apparently contains the Djed, the spine that connects the Judges to the world. And the Shan'iatu sent Azar to Duat. I mean, logically, that means the Judges of Life are now connected to Duat rather than the living world.<br /> <br /> Oh, and speaking of the Djed, one of my favourite implications of the Minor Djed relic is what it means about the city of Irem. The Minor Djed can render an area indestructible and impervious to spiritual forces. The City of Irem was covered in the &quot;full&quot; versions of these things, and the Shan'iatu made it very clear that they intended to take their Empire with them into Duat so that they might enjoy the pleasures of it for all eternity. While the Shan'iatu may not have become the Judges, who's to say that those outside of the Deceived did not descend to Duat as masters of a spiritual kingdom rendered impervious to Duat's demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T05:28:49-07:00","id":665558,"title":"","content":"Still hoping...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T17:17:53-07:00","id":666219,"title":"","content":"I keep forgetting this is even a thing...<br /> <br /> I'm just salivating at the prospect of finally getting my hands on Dreams of Avarice. Really, really hoping we're looking at a PDF release in the next 5-7 weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}